title: One-time code asked for with a lure
severity: high
score: 45
tags: phishing, otp-harvest
attack: T1566.002, T1111
description: A page asks for a one-time code (SMS, Absher, Nafath or bank OTP). It also
  shows a brand or a payment pretext. Or it is on a lookalike or government-lookalike
  domain, on free hosting, or on a domain under 30 days old.
---
// A one-time-code prompt on a page no known brand or allowlisted site runs ...
otp_pages
// ... that imitates a brand, gives a reason to pay, or sits on a lookalike, free-hosted
// or young domain.
| where toscalar(brand_claim | project confidence) >= 35
    or exists(payment_pretext_frames)
    or exists(lookalike_hosts)
    or exists(government_lookalike_hosts)
    or exists(final_free_hosting)
    or toscalar(final_domain | project age_days) < 30
| project url
